Your /todo list is now saved with the session and comes back when you resume it. Committed as b9d96863. Format check, clippy with warnings as errors, and the full test suite all pass. I haven't run a real save-and-resume against a live model. Only the new helper functions are unit-tested; the five call sites themselves are not.

How it works: a session file is a bare list of messages, so there's no field to add the todos to. The list goes in a file next to it instead: .yoyo/last-session.json gets .yoyo/last-session.todos.json.
• **Saved by** /save, auto-save on exit, and --save-session.
• Restored by `/load and --continue`.

Behaviour:
• **Loading replaces the current list.** It's session state, which is the reason @danstis gave for not using a standalone file.
• **IDs carry on:** a new /todo add after a resume never reuses a restored ID.
• **Old sessions** with no todos file resume with an empty list.
• **A corrupt todos file** doesn't stop the resume. You get one warning on stderr and an empty list.
• **Saving an empty list** writes no file and deletes an old one at the same path, so cleared items can't come back. A plain `/save` with no todos still creates only one file.

Tests: I added tests for the full round trip (three items with mixed statuses, checked as a whole list), an old-format session, a corrupt file, and saving an empty list. To check they catch a real failure, I made the restore step do nothing; all four restore tests failed, round trip included. I then put the code back and confirmed no sabotage marker is left.

One change outside the plan: the shell refusal for yoyo todo add said "Persistence across invocations is tracked in #1005". Once this commit closes #1005, that would point users at a closed issue, which is the same mistake fixed on Day 224. It now says the list is saved with the session and comes back on /load or --continue. Its exact-text test was renamed to match, and it now fails if any "tracked in #" pointer comes back.

Docs: docs/src/features/sessions.md describes the todos file and these rules. My first draft said /todo board tasks live under .yoyo/; they're actually in session_plan/, and I fixed that before committing.

The commit message says Fixes #1005 because every save and resume path is covered, so #1005 closes when this is pushed. The issue's third item, reporting back to @danstis in #682, is still owed in the respond phase.
